# AI Secretary — Clean Architecture Rewrite

## Why Rewrite?

The existing code is 100% demo/mock scaffolding. Every tool has hardcoded mock data tangled with real logic, the AI engine crashes on import without an API key, and there's no orchestrator connecting anything. **Patching 5+ files would take longer than a clean rewrite.**

**What we keep**: WAT framework philosophy, workflow [.md](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/CLAUDE.md) files, [.env.template](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/.env.template), [CLAUDE.md](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/CLAUDE.md)
**What we delete**: All [.py](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/web_auth.py) files (they'll be rewritten from scratch)

---

## New Architecture

```
DA Project/
├── main.py                    # Entry point — starts bot + scheduler
├── config.py                  # Centralized config from .env
├── orchestrator.py            # Intent router — the brain
├── tools/
│   ├── outlook_client.py      # Microsoft Graph API (email + calendar)
│   ├── ai_engine.py           # LLM integration (model-agnostic)
│   ├── pdf_generator.py       # HTML → PDF slides
│   └── scheduler.py           # APScheduler with real callbacks
├── bot/
│   └── telegram_handler.py    # Telegram bot with routing + file sending
├── workflows/                 # Kept as-is (markdown SOPs)
├── .env / .env.template
├── CLAUDE.md
└── requirements.txt
```

---

## Proposed Changes

### Core Files

#### [NEW] [config.py](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/config.py)
- Loads all [.env](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/.env) variables in one place
- Validates which services are available (has Azure creds? has OpenAI key? has Telegram token?)
- Provides a single `Config` object used by all components

#### [NEW] [orchestrator.py](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/orchestrator.py)
- Receives natural language from Telegram → classifies intent via AI engine → dispatches to correct tool
- Handles multi-step flows (draft email → show preview → approve/reject → send)
- Returns results as text or files (PDFs) back to Telegram

#### [NEW] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/aabda/OneDrive/Desktop/DA%20Project/main.py)
- Initializes `Config`, all tools, orchestrator, and Telegram bot
- Starts scheduler in background thread
- Runs Telegram polling loop
- Handles graceful shutdown (Ctrl+C)

